## startup: FW boot poll
The cpu-reset retry is NOT new: it appears in both builds (sessions 20261030-001339 and
-002455 on the old radio, 20261030-230721/-232744 on the new one). A timeout costs a full
re-download (~78 s): measured start 2 min 01 s vs 43 s clean.
HalmacJaguar2Fw.cpp is byte-identical between the two bases, so this is pre-existing.
Our fork now polls up to 1 s instead of 250 ms and logs the real boot time at W level:
  FW ready (0x80 = 0xC078) after 8290..21927 us / 1..2 polls  (14 clean starts)
Budget 250 ms was ~30x the observed boot time, so a timeout means the MCU is late or
stalled; 1 s absorbs "late" without changing the wedged case (still retried).

